t-phase","implicit":true,"key":"kMYIRSU2k1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The source and tests retain global phases, which matter when an access is coherently controlled. The pinned Qiskit OpenQASM exporter omits an overall circuit phase. Its measured-trial probabilities remain valid, but the downloaded QASM is not a phase-preserving controlled-oracle specification. Use the source modules or restore the recorded phase for coherent reuse.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"n5KL1XNYZX"}],"key":"FlFJsvkf3D"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The source-operation cap counts top-level instructions; nested definitions and transpilation can consume resources before the primitive-export cap is checked. The default source, projected-block simulation and primitive export are bounded and checked. General source complexity is not validated by a top-level count alone.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"QIe2m3rf8x"}],"key":"RZWq960TbR"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"No inverse channel is used: amplification requires the full unitary access and its inverse. A thermal filter with nonuniform singular values generally changes its target state under oblivious amplification. That method requires a separate distortion/known-input amplification construction. Deterministic amplification, certified rotation synthesis and physical estimates remain planned.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"dqsFXNrK5G"}],"key":"kwjTFtxpWp"}],"identifier":"c4737df8","html_id":"c4737df8","key":"IyX3pcMS7o"}],"key":"OJxWdnKnUb"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"